---
// The services arm is a standalone business, and it should announce itself as
// one. Without this, someone who arrived to evaluate Alex reads a consulting
// storefront and concludes that is the whole identity. A named band at the top,
// a cooler accent underneath it, and the separation does its own explaining.
---

<aside class="practice-bar">
  <div class="pb-mark">
    <span class="pb-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="pb-name">The practice</span>
  </div>
  <p class="pb-what">
    Operations work for small businesses — scoped, priced, and sold on its own.
    <a href="/" class="pb-back">← back to campos.works</a>
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .practice-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--practice-line, rgba(122,164,152,0.28));
    border-left: 2px solid var(--practice-accent, #7aa498);
    background: var(--practice-wash, rgba(122,164,152,0.05));
  }
  .pb-mark { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .pb-dot {
    width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--practice-accent, #7aa498);
    flex: none;
  }
  .pb-name {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--practice-accent, #7aa498);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .pb-what {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--white-60);
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .pb-what a { color: var(--practice-accent, #7aa498); }
  .pb-back { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.74rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; margin-left: 0.6rem; white-space: nowrap; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(122,164,152,0.35); }
  .pb-back:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--practice-accent, #7aa498); }
</style>
